<title>GREECE: Greek shares only 3 pct of 3.87 trn dr fund assets.</title>
<headline>Greek shares only 3 pct of 3.87 trn dr fund assets.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Only 3.0 percent of Greece's 3.87 trillion drachma mutual and closed-end fund assets was invested in domestic equities at year-end 1996, the association of institutional investors said in its yearly review.</p>
<p>The fund industry's assets grew by 1.43 trillion drachmas last year reaching 3.87 trillion in December 31 1996.</p>
<p>The report said the overall asset allocation at year-end 1996 had as follows:</p>
<p>    ASSET			PERCENT</p>
<p>    Greek bonds		61</p>
<p>    Synthetic swaps	  17</p>
<p>    Bank deposits	     7</p>
<p>    Time deposits	     5</p>
<p>    Domestic equities	 3</p>
<p>    Repurchase agreements   3</p>
<p>    Foreign bonds	     2</p>
<p>    Corporate bonds	   1</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
